<a href="/blog/claude-ai-custom-instructions-a-real-example-that-actually-works/" class="featured-card-link"><strong>Claude AI Custom Instructions</strong><br><span style="font-size:0.9em;color:#555">A real example that actually works</span></a></div></aside><aside id="text-7" class="widget widget_text">			<div class="textwidget"><div class="author-box"><strong>About <a href="https://plus.google.com/106282983883202575997?rel=author" rel="author">J.D. Hodges</a></strong><br /><p><img class="alignleft size-thumbnail wp-image-7046" alt="J.D. Hodges Google+ profile photo" src="https://www.jdhodges.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/n26401995_31040552_1268-200x200.jpg" width="100" height="100" />J.D. is an attorney and IT professional living off the grid. He has been a tech enthusiast ever since his dad let him play with computers in the early 80s. Now jdhodges.com is where he shares tech tips. Thanks for visiting & feel free to join in the discussion by commenting :-)
</a></p>
</div></div>
		</aside><aside id="text-11" class="widget widget_text"><h3 class="widgettitle">Solar System</h3>			<div class="textwidget">    <style>
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-rows { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 1px 10px; padding: 0 2px; align-items: baseline; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-lab { white-space: nowrap; font-weight: 700; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-val { white-space: nowrap; text-align: right; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-sub { grid-column: 2; text-align: right; color: #666; font-size: 12px; margin-top: -3px; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-up { color: #1e8449; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-dn { color: #c0392b; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-flat { color: #555; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-w { font-weight: 800; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-word { font-weight: 600; font-size: 12px; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-mut { color: #666; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-title a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-title a:hover, #solar-status-widget .jsw-title a:focus-visible { text-decoration: underline; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-status { font-weight: 600; font-size: 11.5px; margin-left: 4px; vertical-align: middle; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-q { position: absolute; right: 0; top: -2px; width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid #c8d1d9; background: #f4f6f8; color: #444; font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; cursor: pointer; line-height: 1; padding: 0; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-q:hover { background: #e9edf1; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-q:focus-visible, #solar-status-widget .solar-explain-close:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #2471a3; outline-offset: 2px; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-explain { margin: 8px 0 4px; border: 1px solid #d5dbe1; border-radius: 6px; background: #f7f9fa; padding: 10px 12px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.5; color: #333; text-align: left; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-explain dt { font-weight: 700; margin-top: 6px; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-explain dt:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-explain dd { margin: 0 0 2px; color: #4a5560; }
    #solar-status-widget .solar-explain-close { float: right; border: 0; background: none; cursor: pointer; font-size: 13px; color: #666; padding: 2px 4px; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-age a { color: #2471a3; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }
    #solar-status-widget .jsw-age a:hover, #solar-status-widget .jsw-age a:focus-visible { text-decoration: underline; }
    </style>
    <div id="solar-status-widget" style="font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.65;">
        <div class="jsw-title" style="text-align: center; padding: 4px 0 8px; position: relative;">
            <span id="solar-status-dot" style="display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; background: #888; vertical-align: middle;"></span>
            <strong style="vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 4px;"><a href="/solar-system-monitor/">Off-Grid Solar</a></strong>
            <span id="solar-status-word" class="jsw-status"></span>
            <button type="button" class="jsw-q" id="solar-widget-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="About these numbers">?</button>
        </div>
        <div id="solar-soc-headline" style="text-align: center; padding: 0 0 6px; display: none;">
            <span id="solar-soc-value" style="font-size: 28px; font-weight: bold; color: #27ae60;">--%</span>
            <div style="font-size: 11px; color: #666; margin-top: -2px;">Battery SOC</div>
        </div>
        <div class="jsw-explain" id="solar-widget-explain" hidden><button type="button" class="solar-explain-close" aria-label="Close">&#10005;</button><dl style="margin:0;"><dt>Battery SOC</dt><dd>the battery&#039;s fuel gauge (min = today&#039;s lowest).</dd><dt>Battery (net)</dt><dd>what the battery is doing right now: + charging, − draining.</dd><dt>Solar</dt><dd>what the solar panels are producing right now.</dd><dt>Inverter 1 out</dt><dd>power going to the circuits on the main inverter.</dd><dt>Other (net)</dt><dd>everything else combined: the second inverter&#039;s circuits and any external chargers. Inputs and loads can cancel, so this isn&#039;t total usage.</dd><dt>AC / DC</dt><dd>the battery side runs on DC power; house circuits run on AC. The tag on each line says which side you&#039;re looking at.</dd><dt>Solar Chargers</dt><dd>the solar charge controllers&#039; mode. &quot;Silent&quot; just means they&#039;re resting (normal at night).</dd><dt>Last full</dt><dd>how long since the battery was last completely charged.</dd><dt>Green dot / Online</dt><dd>the monitor itself is healthy; &quot;Updated Xs ago&quot; is the reading&#039;s age.</dd></dl></div>
        <div id="solar-status-data" style="padding: 0 4px;">Loading...</div>
        <div id="solar-status-age" class="jsw-age" style="font-size: 11px; color: #666; text-align: center; padding: 5px 0 0;"></div>
    </div>
    <script>
    (function() {
        function esc(s) {
            var d = document.createElement('div');
            d.appendChild(document.createTextNode(String(s)));
            return d.innerHTML;
        }
        function fmt(n) { return n != null ? esc(Math.round(n).toLocaleString()) : '--'; }
        // Derive freshness from the reading timestamp (UTC) instead of trusting
        // the served age_seconds — responses are HTTP-cacheable for up to 30s.
        function deriveAge(d) {
            var t = Date.parse(String(d.timestamp).replace(' ', 'T') + 'Z');
            if (isNaN(t)) return d.age_seconds;
            return Math.max(0, Math.round((Date.now() - t) / 1000));
        }
        var updating = false;
        function update() {
            // Hidden tabs generate zero traffic; visibilitychange refreshes on return
            if (document.hidden || updating) return;
            updating = true;
            fetch('/wp-json/solar-monitor/v1/latest')
                .then(function(r) {
                    if (!r.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + r.status);
                    return r.json();
                })
                .then(function(d) {
                    if (d.status === 'no_data') {
                        document.getElementById('solar-status-data').textContent = 'Awaiting first reading...';
                        return;
                    }
                    var ageSec = deriveAge(d);
                    var liveStatus = ageSec < 180 ? 'online' : ageSec < 600 ? 'stale' : 'offline';
                    var colors = {online: '#2ecc40', stale: '#ff851b', offline: '#ff4136'};
                    document.getElementById('solar-status-dot').style.background = colors[liveStatus] || '#888';
                    // Textual status beside the dot (color-blind safe)
                    var words = {online: ['Online', '#1e8449'], stale: ['Stale', '#a05c00'], offline: ['Offline', '#c0392b']};
                    var wordEl = document.getElementById('solar-status-word');
                    if (words[liveStatus]) {
                        wordEl.textContent = words[liveStatus][0];
                        wordEl.style.color = words[liveStatus][1];
                    } else {
                        wordEl.textContent = '';
                    }

                    // SOC headline
                    var socEl = document.getElementById('solar-soc-headline');
                    var socVal = document.getElementById('solar-soc-value');
                    if (d.battery_soc != null) {
                        socEl.style.display = 'block';
                        var soc = Math.round(d.battery_soc);
                        socVal.textContent = soc + '%';
                        // Color: green > 50, orange 20-50, red < 20
                        socVal.style.color = soc > 50 ? '#27ae60' : soc > 20 ? '#f39c12' : '#e74c3c';
                    } else {
                        socEl.style.display = 'none';
                    }

                    // Coarse W from A x V, rounded to 10W: the rounding IS the
                    // uncertainty disclosure (no tildes by design; tooltips and
                    // the [?] panel carry the estimate language).
                    function approxW(amps) {
                        return Math.round(amps * d.battery_voltage / 10) * 10;
                    }
                    // Round BEFORE choosing the sign: (-0).toLocaleString() is "-0"
                    // and (-0.04).toFixed(1) is "-0.0" — normalize both to plain 0.
                    function signedW(w) {
                        var r = Math.round(w);
                        if (r === 0) r = 0;
                        return (r > 0 ? '+' : '') + r.toLocaleString() + 'W';
                    }
                    function signedA(a) {
                        var v = a.toFixed(1);
                        if (v === '-0.0') v = '0.0';
                        return (parseFloat(v) > 0 ? '+' : '') + v + 'A';
                    }

                    var rows = '';
                    function row(emoji, label, tip, valueHtml) {
                        rows += '<span class="jsw-lab"' + (tip ? ' title="' + tip + '"' : '') + '><span aria-hidden="true">' + emoji + '</span> ' + label + '</span><span class="jsw-val">' + valueHtml + '</span>';
                    }

                    // Battery (net): bold signed W + word; balanced band |W| < 50
                    var vTxt = esc(d.battery_voltage) + 'V DC';
                    if (d.battery_current != null && d.battery_voltage > 0) {
                        var bw = approxW(d.battery_current);
                        var cls = bw >= 50 ? 'jsw-up' : bw <= -50 ? 'jsw-dn' : 'jsw-flat';
                        var word = bw >= 50 ? 'charging' : bw <= -50 ? 'draining' : 'balanced';
                        row('\u26a1', 'Battery (net)', 'Net battery power: every charging and draining path combined',
                            '<span class="jsw-w ' + cls + '">' + esc(signedW(bw)) + '</span> <span class="jsw-word ' + cls + '">' + word + '</span>');
                        rows += '<span class="jsw-sub">' + vTxt + ' \u00b7 ' + esc(signedA(d.battery_current)) + '</span>';
                    } else {
                        row('\u26a1', 'Battery (net)', 'Net battery power: every charging and draining path combined', vTxt);
                    }
                    row('\u2600\ufe0f', 'Solar', 'Solar panel production right now', fmt(d.solar_watts) + 'W');
                    var invVal = fmt(d.house_load_watts) + 'W';
                    if (d.ac_output_voltage != null) {
                        invVal += ' \u00b7 ' + esc(Math.round(d.ac_output_voltage)) + 'V AC';
                    }
                    row('\ud83c\udfe0', 'Inverter 1 out', 'Main inverter AC output only; its amp telemetry is whole-number, so watts are approximate. Other circuits appear under Other (net).', invVal);
                    if (d.aux_net_amps != null && d.battery_voltage > 0) {
                        var aw = approxW(d.aux_net_amps);
                        row('\ud83d\udd0c', 'Other (net)', 'Net of all other chargers and loads (estimate): positive = outside power coming in, negative = extra loads drawing',
                            esc(signedW(aw)) + ' <span class="jsw-mut">\u00b7 ' + esc(signedA(d.aux_net_amps)) + ' DC</span>');
                    }
                    row('\ud83d\udcca', 'Solar today', 'Solar energy produced so far today', esc(d.solar_daily_kwh) + ' kWh');
                    row('\ud83d\udd06', 'Solar Chargers', 'Solar charge controller mode; external chargers are not reflected here', esc(d.charge_state));
                    if (d.days_since_full != null) {
                        rows += '<span class="jsw-sub">last full ' + esc(d.days_since_full.toFixed(1)) + 'd ago</span>';
                    }

                    document.getElementById('solar-status-data').innerHTML = '<div class="jsw-rows">' + rows + '</div>';

                    var ageText = ageSec < 60 ? ageSec + 's ago' :
                                  ageSec < 3600 ? Math.floor(ageSec/60) + 'm ago' :
                                  Math.floor(ageSec/3600) + 'h ago';
                    document.getElementById('solar-status-age').innerHTML = 'Updated ' + esc(ageText) + ' \u00b7 <a href="/solar-system-monitor/">View charts \u2192</a>';
                })
                .catch(function() {
                    document.getElementById('solar-status-dot').style.background = '#ff4136';
                    document.getElementById('solar-status-word').textContent = '';
                    document.getElementById('solar-status-age').textContent = 'Connection error';
                })
                .then(function() { updating = false; });
        }
        // [?] explainer: real button (hover titles don't exist on phones)
        var qBtn = document.getElementById('solar-widget-q');
        var qPanel = document.getElementById('solar-widget-explain');
        if (qBtn && qPanel) {
            var qToggle = function(open) {
                qPanel.hidden = !open;
                qBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(open));
            };
            qBtn.addEventListener('click', function() { qToggle(qPanel.hidden); });
            qPanel.querySelector('.solar-explain-close').addEventListener('click', function() { qToggle(false); qBtn.focus(); });
            document.addEventListener('keydown', function(e) {
                if (e.key === 'Escape' && !qPanel.hidden) { qToggle(false); qBtn.focus(); }
            });
        }

        update();
        // 300s cadence: this widget renders sitewide, and 60s polling from every
        // open tab was 141k req/day (60% of server load, 2026-08-05 incident).
        setInterval(update, 300000);
        document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', function() {
            if (!document.hidden) update();
        });
    })();
    </script>
    </div>
		</aside><aside id="text-12" class="widget widget_text"><h3 class="widgettitle">Indoor Temps</h3>			<div class="textwidget">    <div id="temp-status-widget" style="font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7;">
        <div style="text-align: center; padding: 4px 0 8px;">
            <span id="temp-status-dot" style="display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; background: #888; vertical-align: middle;"></span>
            <strong style="vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 4px;">Indoor Temps</strong>
        </div>
        <div id="temp-status-data" style="padding: 0 4px;">Loading...</div>
        <div id="temp-status-age" style="font-size: 11px; color: #888; text-align: center; padding: 4px 0;"></div>
    </div>
    <script>
    (function() {
        function esc(s) {
            var d = document.createElement('div');
            d.appendChild(document.createTextNode(String(s)));
            return d.innerHTML;
        }
        var updating = false;
        function update() {
            // Hidden tabs generate zero traffic (2026-08-05 incident: sitewide
            // widget polling was 60% of server load with solar-monitor)
            if (document.hidden || updating) return;
            updating = true;
            fetch('/wp-json/temp-monitor/v1/latest')
                .then(function(r) { return r.json(); })
                .then(function(d) {
                    if (d.status === 'no_data') {
                        document.getElementById('temp-status-data').textContent = 'Awaiting first reading...';
                        return;
                    }
                    var colors = {online: '#2ecc40', stale: '#ff851b', offline: '#ff4136'};
                    document.getElementById('temp-status-dot').style.background = colors[d.status] || '#888';

                    var html = '';
                    var lastSite = '';
                    d.sensors.forEach(function(s) {
                        if (s.site !== lastSite) {
                            if (lastSite !== '') html += '<div style="height: 4px;"></div>';
                            lastSite = s.site;
                        }
                        var temp = s.temperature != null ? esc(s.temperature.toFixed(1)) + '&deg;F' : '--';
                        var hum = s.humidity != null ? esc(s.humidity.toFixed(0)) + '%' : '--';

                        // Color code temperature
                        var tempColor = '#333';
                        if (s.temperature != null) {
                            if (s.temperature > 85) tempColor = '#e74c3c';
                            else if (s.temperature > 75) tempColor = '#f39c12';
                            else if (s.temperature < 50) tempColor = '#3498db';
                            else tempColor = '#27ae60';
                        }

                        html += '<div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline;">';
                        html += '<span>' + esc(s.name) + '</span>';
                        html += '<span><b style="color:' + tempColor + ';">' + temp + '</b>';
                        html += ' <span style="font-size:11px;color:#888;">' + hum + ' RH</span></span>';
                        html += '</div>';
                    });

                    document.getElementById('temp-status-data').innerHTML = html;

                    var age = d.age_seconds;
                    var ageText = age < 60 ? age + 's ago' :
                                  age < 3600 ? Math.floor(age/60) + 'm ago' :
                                  Math.floor(age/3600) + 'h ago';
                    document.getElementById('temp-status-age').textContent = 'Updated ' + ageText;
                })
                .catch(function() {
                    document.getElementById('temp-status-dot').style.background = '#ff4136';
                    document.getElementById('temp-status-age').textContent = 'Connection error';
                })
                .then(function() { updating = false; });
        }
        update();
        setInterval(update, 300000);
        document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', function() {
            if (!document.hidden) update();
        });
    })();
    </script>
    
</div>
